okay let's get into audience questions  the first one one that i am asked so  often david why does it appear to be  more profitable to be a right-wing  grifter  than it does to be a left-wing grifter  either someone who  pretends to have changed sides or have a  political awakening or simply put out  ideas that even they don't believe  merely because it makes money there are  two reasons why  right wing grifting is so much more  popular than left wing grifting  the uh the the two reasons are number  one  the left doesn't really care about  people who have these opposite  supposed awakenings or come to  realize that what they've been fed by  their side is wrong or whatever the left  doesn't care about it in the same  way and number two there's just less  money available on the left for it so  we'll explain these one by one the idea  of someone who used to be on the left  and now is on the right as someone we  should pay particular attention to  is much more exciting to the right the  left doesn't care  people call into the show all the time  and say i had an awakening  i'm on the left now i used to be a right  winger i fell down the rabbit hole  it's interesting in the sense that i'm  curious how did you get out because we  know it's tough to get out  but my reaction is a very muted oh so  you looked at the facts and now you  better understand things you're no  longer falling for propaganda  you now understand the real world and so  of course now you're on the same side  i'm on which is the site of empiricism  and facts and so on and so forth  now let's try to get something done  let's get the right people elected let's  try to fix some some problems in society  what you see on the right is completely  different when dave rubin  supposedly had an awakening from being a  bernie guy  to saying liberalism is a mental  disorder he was  ushered into prageru to do a video about  how he left the left  when candace owens i mean candace owen's  story is a little more nuanced because  for identity reasons she's also really  interesting to the right but  she has this story it may be real it may  be not how she grew up in a democratic  house and i think it was connecticut or  whatever and then she figured out all  these things  the right sees that and they celebrate  it in some kind of defiant heroic  reaction whereas the left when when it  happens just says oh you were you were  uninformed great now  now you're now you're with us but let's  go to the next thing  it's not it's just not as interesting to  the audiences and  case in point many people may not  remember  jenk yuger has taught host to the young  turks has talked about how  when he was young he was a reactionary  conservative republican he was i think  in the republican  club in college whatever every once in a  while it comes up but it essentially has  nothing to do with the success of the  young turks like the young turks or not  it's not predicated on this heroic  awakening that jenk had which could be a  grift or it might not and he  was like yeah it seems pretty clear he  was kind of a moderate republican in  in college and now he's not okay that's  it so the right creates cults of  personality around these people  in the way that left doesn't and it  makes it really appealing financially  okay second piece money  there just is more money available for  this stuff  on the right than there is on the left  i'll i've i've seen it firsthand and  we've dealt with all sorts of different  groups and  there just is on the right there are  tons of well-funded groups  that love to throw money at people who  are  doing the grift so to speak um these  libertarian groups that pay to bring  people to college campuses and you can  get  nice speaking fees uh depending on your  level your profile  you know the speaking fee can can be  more or less there really isn't much of  that  on the left uh the few times i've been  paid to speak at colleges it was that  the college had like a donor-funded  thing of  let's bring people to speak there were  never groups  in fact whenever i get invited by  left-leaning groups they say we have no  money  um organizations that then will  fund you know interview series on  different programs and these types of  things  uh donations as well even just  soliciting  the enlightened centrism tim poole as an  example who raised  a ton of money as someone who said he  was like mostly a bernie guy and all  this stuff but  then 90 percent of his content became  criticizing the left and praising trump  he raised a whole bunch of money with  the idea that he  who had he was on one side but he sees  this and the other and now he's got this  whole nice  neat little package as the arbiter of  what's what's right and what's wrong  um he was able to raise a ton of money  on the idea of launching  such a website that would just give you  the news  tm some they figured out how to do the  news and people donated like crazy to it  that appeals to  to right wingers um and i know someone  will say oh left i'm a left winger i  donated to that okay fine but  the the left does not reward that that  stuff that type of grifting um  ideologically  in terms of the cults of personality  around people  nor financially that's the explanation  as i see it that's the explanation as  i've  experienced it from within and remember  i told the story  of this radio consultant who met with me  years ago and said you know  do you really care about like what  you're saying because if you just want  to be a performer  there is a need right now for shows like  yours or you know  at the time a really young guy but on  the right i could get you syndicated and  we could triple your salary  and i've told that story before there  was no such thing available to me on the  left  um and i'm glad i turned it down and  everything worked out fine no regrets  whatsoever so those are my thoughts on  the profitability  of the left-wing grift versus the  right-wing grift or the lack thereof  when it comes to the left-wing grift  send me more thoughts about what you  think might uh explain that difference
 

